  "editorialSummary": "Nothing says peak efficiency quite like global markets [reeling from tech sell-offs](https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/20/business/anthropic-ai-stocks-sp500.html) while diplomats scramble over [Ukraine peace talks](https://www.latercera.com/mundo/noticia/eeuu-insiste-en-que-rusia-se-comprometio-a-un-formato-multilateral-de-negociaciones-con-europe/)[and COP31 climate deadlock](https://www.lemonde.fr/en/environment/article/2026/11/20/cop31-fossil-fuels-and-climate-funding-take-center-stage-in-final-stretch-of-negociaciones_6785737_114.html). At least mathematicians celebrating the [Riemann hypothesis breakthrough](https://www.newscientist.com/article/2600134-anthropic-mathematician-claims-ai-assisted-proof-of-the-riemann-hypothesis/?utm_campaign=RSS|NSNS&utm_content=home&utm_medium=RSS&utm_source=NSNS) finally have an equation complex enough to calculate how much worse tomorrow gets.",
